// extdeps/languages/python/primitives.dag — Structural target-primitive
// declarations for the Python target (T-Ground-Python tranche 1 / spec authority).
//
// FIRST SLICE (this file): Python language-reference built-in types whose
// value domain is fixed by the language spec — `int` (arbitrary precision),
// `bool`, `str` (immutable Unicode code-point sequence), and `None` (the
// single inhabitant of `NoneType`). See Python Language Reference §"The
// standard type hierarchy" (docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html) and
// §"Numeric Types — int, float, complex"
// (docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#numeric-types-int-float-complex).
//
// `float` and `complex` are intentionally omitted from this tranche: the
// language reference states "Floating point numbers are usually implemented
// using double in C" and explicitly flags float/complex precision as
// "implementation dependent". Declaring a fixed IEEE-754 carrier here would
// repeat the same no-lying-about-width discipline violation Go's omission of
// `int` / `uint` / `uintptr` calls out — defer until a CPython-tagged
// implementation-width story lands alongside DB-11 / cardinality substrate.
// `bytes` / `bytearray` (built-in byte-sequence types) are also deferred to
// the next tranche; they're language-level but not part of the
// numeric/bool/str tranche-1 scope per dispatch brief.
//
// TWO-AUTHORITY DISCIPLINE (ROADMAP §Post-R1 Grounding lanes):
//   (a) THIS FILE — Python language reference (docs.python.org/3/reference).
//   (b) stdlib carriers and product-specific rows (e.g. `dict` for Json,
//       `bytes` for Bytes payloads consumed via stdlib paths) stay in
//       python/types.dag + emit tables until a dedicated stdlib-authority
//       slice lands; do not cite stdlib paths here.
//
// CONSUMER BOUNDARY: top-level list / record aggregates lower structurally.
// What is *not* yet live for this file: there is no Python-grounding consumer
// in-tree yet for `python_spec_predeclared_primitives` or
// `python_dag_unit_target_primitive` — so today these rows are loaded but
// unconsumed (Path-2 staging in the fixture-registration sense, not in the
// lowering sense). Type-structure (`PythonPrimitive = …`) is walkable for the
// future engine consumer.
//
// LESSON 5 (grounding-pilot-receipt.md): subset-only axes are structurally
// partitioned — every `PythonPrimitive` variant carries its own per-variant
// algebra-tag and carrier-tag witness types, so any algebra/carrier pair
// other than the spec-valid one is unrepresentable by construction (no
// `PythonBooleanPrimitive { algebra: TerminalAlgebra }`,
// no `PythonIntegerPrimitive { carrier: BitCarrier }`).
//
// STRING (language ref §"Text Sequence Type — str",
// docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#textseq): a `str` value is an
// immutable sequence of Unicode code points (free monoid over Unicode code
// points). Source-text encoding (UTF-8 / UTF-16 / etc.) is NOT a second
// carrier/algebra authority on the spec `str` row — it is encode/decode
// surface and belongs in operator or stdlib slices, not parallel sum arms
// on `PythonStringPrimitive`. (Same discipline as Go's spec-string row
// declining a UTF-8 parallel authority on `GoStringPrimitive`.)
//
// SUBSTRATE-GAP FLAGS:
//   1. Python `int` is arbitrary precision — no fixed-width carrier and no
//      modular-wrap overflow. This file models it with the
//      `PythonIntUnboundedCarrier` sentinel (no `range_min/max`,
//      no `overflow` field) so consumers cannot read a false fixed width.
//      Post-DB-11 / cardinality substrate this becomes
//      `OrderedRing<UnboundedSignedInteger>` with countably-infinite
//      cardinality; today the sentinel carrier is the honest declaration.
//   2. `bool` is a subclass of `int` per the Python data model
//      (True == 1, False == 0). This file routes `bool` through
//      `PythonBooleanPrimitive` with the canonical two-element Boolean
//      algebra value-domain (Bit-carrier sentinel) and does not yet model
//      the int-coercion edge — that lives in coercion / operator slices,
//      not on the predeclared primitive row.
//   3. Algebra and carrier identity is still carried by structural tags
//      (per-variant `Python<Variant>SpecAlgebraTag` /
//      `Python<Variant>SpecCarrierTag`), same bridge pattern as
//      rust/primitives.dag and go/primitives.dag, until the .dag substrate
//      exposes type expressions as data values.

module extdeps.languages.python.primitives

// =========================================================================
// Per-variant algebra / carrier witness tags.
//
// State-space modeling discipline: each `PythonPrimitive` variant gets its
// own dedicated algebra-tag and carrier-tag sum, so the spec-valid
// (algebra, carrier) pair is the *only* representable assignment for that
// row. Sharing a broad `PythonNonIntegerAlgebra` across Boolean and Unit
// (or a broad `PythonTargetCarrier` across Integer / Boolean / Unit) would
// admit nonsense rows like `PythonBooleanPrimitive { algebra: TerminalAlgebra }`
// — illegal-states-unrepresentable forbids that.
//
// Coproduct-dissolution ledger annotations follow the
// post-#1046 Go file style: each closed coproduct names its **🟢 GREEN**
// (terminal / consumed) arm and its **🟡 YELLOW** (parse-scaffold reserved)
// arm. Every coproduct below has ≥2 arms by construction (v2 bootstrap
// loader rejects unary `type X = Tag` aliases), with reserved arms named
// for their dissolution trigger: bootstrap / loader closes single-arm sums,
// at which point the reserved arms (and these per-variant tag types
// entirely) collapse into direct algebra/carrier references — see
// substrate-gap flag #3.
// =========================================================================

// --- Integer primitive witness tags ---
//
// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonIntOrderedRingAlgebra` is the terminal
// algebra-tag for Python's spec integer (signed, additive inverse exists).
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonIntegerSpecAlgebraReserved`.
type PythonIntegerSpecAlgebraTag
  = PythonIntOrderedRingAlgebra
  | PythonIntegerSpecAlgebraReserved

// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonIntUnboundedCarrier` is the honest
// declaration that Python `int` is arbitrary-precision (substrate-gap
// flag #1; DB-11 will refine to a countably-infinite cardinality witness).
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonIntegerSpecCarrierReserved`.
type PythonIntegerSpecCarrierTag
  = PythonIntUnboundedCarrier
  | PythonIntegerSpecCarrierReserved


// --- Boolean primitive witness tags ---
//
// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonBoolCanonicalTwoElementBooleanAlgebra`
// is the terminal algebra-tag for Python's spec `bool`.
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonBooleanSpecAlgebraReserved`.
type PythonBooleanSpecAlgebraTag
  = PythonBoolCanonicalTwoElementBooleanAlgebra
  | PythonBooleanSpecAlgebraReserved

// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonBoolBitCarrier` is the algebra
// value-domain witness for `bool` (per `dsl/std/integer.dag:4` carrier-vs-
// evidence convention; not CPython object representation).
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonBooleanSpecCarrierReserved`.
type PythonBooleanSpecCarrierTag
  = PythonBoolBitCarrier
  | PythonBooleanSpecCarrierReserved


// --- String primitive witness tags ---
//
// **🟢 GREEN** —
// `PythonStrImmutableUnicodeCodePointSequenceMonoidAlgebra` is the
// terminal algebra-tag for Python `str` (header §STRING).
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonStringSpecAlgebraReserved`. Encoding
// (UTF-8 / UTF-16) is NOT a second arm here.
type PythonStringSpecAlgebraTag
  = PythonStrImmutableUnicodeCodePointSequenceMonoidAlgebra
  | PythonStringSpecAlgebraReserved

// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonStrUnicodeCodePointSequenceCarrier` is
// the terminal carrier-tag for Python `str`.
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonStringSpecCarrierReserved`.
type PythonStringSpecCarrierTag
  = PythonStrUnicodeCodePointSequenceCarrier
  | PythonStringSpecCarrierReserved


// --- Unit (None / NoneType) primitive witness tags ---
//
// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonUnitTerminalAlgebra` is the
// single-inhabitant algebra of `NoneType`.
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonUnitSpecAlgebraReserved`.
type PythonUnitSpecAlgebraTag
  = PythonUnitTerminalAlgebra
  | PythonUnitSpecAlgebraReserved

// **🟢 GREEN** — `PythonUnitTerminalCarrier` is the
// single-inhabitant carrier sentinel for `None` (DB-11 will refine to
// `Cardinality<T, Exactly(1)>`).
// **🟡 YELLOW (scaffold)** — `PythonUnitSpecCarrierReserved`.
type PythonUnitSpecCarrierTag
  = PythonUnitTerminalCarrier
  | PythonUnitSpecCarrierReserved


// =========================================================================
// Sum-typed Python spec primitive (Lesson 5 partition).
//
// Sum-typed so each spec primitive's structurally-meaningful axes attach
// only where they have meaning, AND each variant's algebra/carrier fields
// are typed by per-variant singleton-tag pairs (see witness-tag block
// above) — illegal-states-unrepresentable: a `PythonBooleanPrimitive` can
// only carry `PythonBoolCanonicalTwoElementBooleanAlgebra` and
// `PythonBoolBitCarrier`; a `PythonIntegerPrimitive` can only carry
// `PythonIntOrderedRingAlgebra` and `PythonIntUnboundedCarrier`; etc.
//
// No `range_min/max` and no `overflow` field on `PythonIntegerPrimitive`:
// substrate-gap flag #1 — Python's spec `int` is unbounded, so a
// fixed-range / fixed-overflow row would be a lie. Consumers needing
// concrete-width integer routing should consult target-specific lanes
// (Rust / Go `*_integer_range` rows) rather than synthesizing a width here.
//
// **🟡 YELLOW (scheduled
// scaffold).** All four arms are spec-realized and consumed today (each
// has a matching row in `python_spec_predeclared_primitives` /
// `python_dag_unit_target_primitive`):
//   - `PythonIntegerPrimitive` ↔ row `int` (spec §"Numeric Types" — int).
//   - `PythonBooleanPrimitive` ↔ row `bool` (spec §"Boolean Type — bool").
//   - `PythonStringPrimitive`  ↔ row `str`  (spec §"Text Sequence — str").
//   - `PythonUnitPrimitive`    ↔ row `None` (spec §"The Null Object — None").
// The partition itself is YELLOW (not GREEN) because its end-state is
// dissolution, not steady-state coexistence: when DB-11 / cardinality
// substrate lets algebra+carrier be referenced as data, all four variants
// collapse into a single record-shaped row with refinement-typed fields,
// and `PythonPrimitive` retires alongside the per-variant witness tags.
// Dissolution trigger: DB-11 / cardinality substrate (named).
// =========================================================================

type PythonPrimitive
  = PythonIntegerPrimitive {
      target_name: String
      algebra: PythonIntegerSpecAlgebraTag
      carrier: PythonIntegerSpecCarrierTag
    }
  | PythonStringPrimitive {
      target_name: String
      algebra: PythonStringSpecAlgebraTag
      carrier: PythonStringSpecCarrierTag
    }
  | PythonBooleanPrimitive {
      target_name: String
      algebra: PythonBooleanSpecAlgebraTag
      carrier: PythonBooleanSpecCarrierTag
    }
  | PythonUnitPrimitive {
      target_name: String
      algebra: PythonUnitSpecAlgebraTag
      carrier: PythonUnitSpecCarrierTag
    }


// Predeclared spec primitives: int, bool, str.
// (None / NoneType is split into a separate top-level row below — same
// pattern as Go's `go_dag_unit_target_primitive` — because `None` is the
// canonical DAG `Unit` realization in `python/types.dag`, not a numeric
// or sequence primitive.)
//
// `float` / `complex` deferred (header §implementation-defined width).
// `bytes` / `bytearray` deferred to next tranche.
data python_spec_predeclared_primitives: List<PythonPrimitive> = [
  PythonIntegerPrimitive { target_name: "int",
    algebra: PythonIntOrderedRingAlgebra,
    carrier: PythonIntUnboundedCarrier },

  PythonBooleanPrimitive { target_name: "bool",
    algebra: PythonBoolCanonicalTwoElementBooleanAlgebra,
    carrier: PythonBoolBitCarrier },

  PythonStringPrimitive { target_name: "str",
    algebra: PythonStrImmutableUnicodeCodePointSequenceMonoidAlgebra,
    carrier: PythonStrUnicodeCodePointSequenceCarrier }
]

// DAG Unit → Python: `None` (the sole inhabitant of `NoneType`) is the
// target spelling for DagName `Unit` in `python/types.dag`. Split out from
// the predeclared list (same pattern as `go_dag_unit_target_primitive`)
// because `None` is a value, not a type name in the spec's predeclared-type
// list — `NoneType` is the type and is not a builtin identifier in the
// scope a user can name without `types.NoneType`. The target-name string
// here records the value spelling consumers emit ("None"), aligning with
// `python_type_checkpoints` in `python/types.dag`.
data python_dag_unit_target_primitive: PythonPrimitive = PythonUnitPrimitive {
  target_name: "None",
  algebra: PythonUnitTerminalAlgebra,
  carrier: PythonUnitTerminalCarrier
}
